  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Natarajan vs State on 28 July, 2020 Author: V.Bharathidasan Bench: V.Bharathidasan Crl.O.P.(M Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court ( Criminal Jurisdiction ) Dated : 28/07/2020 Present The Hon`ble Mr.Justice V.Bharathidasan CRL.O.P.(MD)No.7342 of 2020 1.Natarajan 2.Ayyanar : Petition Vs. State, through the Inspector of Police, Mudukulathur Police Station, Ramanathapuram District. (Crime No.389 of 2020) . : Responde",
    "facts": "The petitioners moved a petition seeking bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure before the learned Principal District and Sessions Judge, Ramanathapuram. 3. According to the petitioners, due to lock down owing to COVID-19 pandemic situation, as they are residing at Salem District, they could not get entry passes to enter Ramanathapuram District from the District Administration and now the petitioners executed the sureties and are reporting before the respondent police for 13 days and as it would be difficult for the petitioners to appear before the respondent police daily, they have come forward with the present petition seeking modification of the said condition. 4.",
    "arguments": "2. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioners would submit that the petitioners were arrested and remanded to judicial custody on 23.06.2020 in connection with a case registered in Crime No.389 of 2020 on the file of the respondent police for the alleged offences punishable under Sections 120-B, 188, 269, 270, 273, 328, 417 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 7, 20(1), 20(2) of the Cigarette and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003 and Sections 52 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. The learned counsel appearing for the petitioners would submit that the petitioners were arrested and remanded to judicial custody on 23.06.2020 in connection with a case registered in Crime No.389 of 2020 on the file of the respondent police for the alleged offences punishable under Sections 120-B, 188, 269, 270, 273, 328, 417 of the Indian Penal Code and Sections 7, 20(1), 20(2) of the Cigarette and other Tobacco Products Act, 2003 and Sections 52 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
